rs/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":3687,"state":"closed","created_at":"2024-12-19T08:51:28Z","updated_at":"2026-09-04T21:48:38Z","due_on":"2025-09-15T00:00:00Z","closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-05-12T19:35:20Z","updated_at":"2025-05-13T21:28:22Z","closed_at":"2025-05-13T21:28:00Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/106319","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106319","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106319.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106319.patch","merged_at":"2025-05-13T21:28:00Z"},"body":"This PR adds WebAssembly [SIMD](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Single_instruction,_multiple_data) support (by default).\r\nThis new option is a boolean named `wasm_simd=[yes|no]`.\r\n\r\nSIMD improves CPU performance **by a lot** when supported. Pretty important when most Web games run single threaded.\r\n\r\nFrom [Can I Use...](https://caniuse.com/wasm-simd), it seems that WebAssembly SIMD is supported on major browsers for about two years now. The [Wonderland Engine](https://wonderlandengine.com/) (a game engine optimized for the Web) [just announced](https://wonderlandengine.com/news/release-1.4.0/#always-simd) that they drop support for non-SIMD exports on their latest release, arguing that SIMD support is pretty much a given nowadays.\r\n\r\n### Demos\r\n| Demo name | without SIMD | with SIMD |\r\n| :---: | :---: | :---: |\r\n| Jolt Physics<br>(with @passivestar's demo) | https://adamscott.github.io/godot-physics-demo-without-simd/ | https://adamscott.github.io/godot-physics-demo-with-simd/ |\r\n| Array copy | https://adamscott.github.io/godot-array-copy-without-simd/ | https://adamscott.github.io/godot-array-copy-with-simd/ |\r\n\r\n> [!NOTE]\r\n> I promised I would shoutout @Squareys (Jonathan Hale from the Wonderland Engine) for the suggestion. It seems that using SIMD really does a difference.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106319/reactions","total_count":45,"+1":21,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":6,"confused":0,"heart":6,"rocket":12,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106319/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}